## Everyday tasks (all done inside the website)

**Add a teacher or staff member**
Menu → **Teachers & staff** → **Add person**. Enter their name, email, and a
temporary password. Tell them those details — they sign in and can change the
password later.

**Reset someone's password**
Menu → **Teachers & staff** → **Reset password** next to their name. Type a new
temporary password and tell them.

**Someone leaves the school**
Menu → **Teachers & staff** → **Disable** next to their name. This blocks their
login but keeps everything they entered. **Don't delete people** — disabling is
the correct, safe action.

**Add or update students**
Menu → **Students**. To remove a student who has left, use **Archive**, not
delete — their school record must be kept.

---

## Backups — please read
This system holds student records, so a backup is not optional.

- **Best option:** turn on **Supabase Pro** (about $25/month). It takes an
  automatic backup every day and you never think about it again. For a system
  the school depends on, this is worth it.
- **Free option:** once a month, log into Supabase → your project →
  **Database → Backups** (or **Database → Backups / Export**) and download a
  copy. Keep it somewhere safe (school drive + a second location).

---

## "The project is paused" (only on the free plan)
If the system has not been used for about a week (e.g. a long holiday), the free
Supabase plan pauses it. Nothing is lost. To bring it back: log into Supabase,
open the project, and click **Resume / Restore**. It's back in a minute or two.
Upgrading to Pro removes this entirely.

---

## If something breaks
Don't worry and don't change settings. Hire any web developer for an hour and
give them the file **DEPLOY.md** (in this folder) — it explains exactly how the
system is set up and how to fix or redeploy it.

---

## What it costs
- **Today:** free.
- **Recommended:** about **$25/month** for Supabase Pro once this is the school's
  real record-keeping system (daily backups + never pauses). Everything else
  stays free.
